From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:09:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/23] teflon,rocket: give partitions without a convolution
 back to the CPU

Whether an operation is worth claiming can depend on the rest of the
graph: on RK3576 a partition of claimed operations that contains no
convolution, such as a lone ADD in the CPU post-processing of MoveNet or
YOLOX, costs an NPU round trip (submit, wait and two layout conversions)
for an operation the CPU does in microseconds. ml_operation_supported
sees one operation at a time and cannot tell.

Add an optional pipe_context::ml_operations_filter, which Teflon calls
once per graph with every operation in execution order and the result of
ml_operation_supported for each; the driver may give operations back.
Drivers that do not set it are unchanged.

Rocket sets it on RK3576. It computes the partitions the way TFLite's
PartitionGraphIntoIndependentNodeSubsets() does (greedy, in execution
order) and gives back the operations of every partition without a
convolution or fully connected layer, repeating until nothing changes,
as giving operations back changes the partitions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6ragSxZN7WKWgGsfgrMX1
